RUN 26 CONTROLLER BEHAVIOUR DISPOSITION
source: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompt_graph_controller.py (2110 lines, read for reference only, not copied)
target: plans/27_langgraph_curriculum_factory_remediation/controller/ (core.py, scheduler.py, run27_controller.py, contracts.py, check_forbidden_production_refs.py, verify_*.py)

Disposition vocabulary:
  RETAINED  the behaviour is correct and is reimplemented in the Run 27 controller
  REPLACED  the behaviour was necessary but defective; a different mechanism now serves the same purpose
  REJECTED  the behaviour is not carried forward at all

--- RETAINED ---------------------------------------------------------------
R01 RETAINED  sha256_bytes / sha256_file streaming file hashing            -> core.sha256_bytes, core.sha256_file
R02 RETAINED  canonical_digest over sort_keys JSON                         -> core.canonical_digest / core.canonical_text
R03 RETAINED  write-once artifact creation via open(path, "x")             -> core.write_once_text / core.write_once_json (now raises WRITE_ONCE_VIOLATION)
R04 RETAINED  atomic single-rename file replacement (staged temp + os.replace) -> core.atomic_write_text
R05 RETAINED  append-only JSONL event stream                               -> core.append_jsonl; state audit.jsonl plus per-attempt events.jsonl
R06 RETAINED  covers() / paths_overlap() path-ownership predicates         -> core.covers, core.paths_overlap
R07 RETAINED  topological_order and descendants graph traversals           -> Graph.order, Graph.descendants, Graph.ancestors
R08 RETAINED  ephemeral-name/suffix ignore list for tree snapshots         -> core.is_ephemeral, core.tree_digest
R09 RETAINED  per-node receipt store with history archive of superseded receipts -> Scheduler.receipt_path + receipts/history/<node>/<sha>.json
R10 RETAINED  write-set enforcement against the node's declared writes     -> Scheduler.validate_node_result WRITE_SET_VIOLATION (now evaluated before any merge journal)
R11 RETAINED  rerunning the graph's own verification commands and recording exit codes -> Scheduler.run_verification, receipt.verification[]
R12 RETAINED  binding predecessor state into the receipt                   -> receipt.predecessor_receipts (scheduler receipt digests) and receipt.predecessor_results (node-declared result digests)
R13 RETAINED  one attempt directory per attempt                            -> state/attempts/<node_id>/<attempt_id>/, now immutable
R14 RETAINED  node_definition digest covering the node entry plus graph rules -> Graph.node_definition_digest

--- REPLACED ---------------------------------------------------------------
P01 REPLACED  _node_reported_status(): scraping a bare "status: X" line out of the node's stdout/Markdown.
              PM-17. Replaced by core.load_node_result: strict json.loads plus Draft 2020-12 validation against the frozen
              schemas/node_result.schema.v1.json, then result["outcome"]. Non-JSON input fails with NON_JSON_RESULT and can
              never produce a receipt. Proven by tests/test_node_result_protocol.py::test_markdown_and_prose_cannot_report_a_status.
P02 REPLACED  ReceiptStore.mechanically_revalidate(): silently admitting a receipt whose input_fingerprint no longer matched.
              PM-15/PM-19. Replaced by an explicit, named readmit operation requiring a reason code from a closed enum, an exact
              --expect-result-sha256 artifact binding, a forced verification rerun, and an immutable audit event.
P03 REPLACED  stored input_fingerprint compared with tolerance.
              PM-15. Replaced by Scheduler.currency(): recomputed on every read from graph digest, node definition, prompt,
              approved specification, predecessor receipt digests, own final-output digests, and recursive ancestor currency.
              A receipt can never be stale-but-flagged-valid because nothing is stored as a validity flag.
P04 REPLACED  _merge(): copying an entire sandbox workspace into the main repository path by path, with a premerge backup
              manifest and per-path rollback, which produced 5 merge rollbacks and one merge completed after interruption.
              PM-19. Replaced by a single-file journaled merge: pending_merge.json (write-once, carrying both the new receipt
              bytes and the previous receipt bytes), then exactly one os.replace of the receipt file, then a write-once
              merged.json. There is no multi-file window, so no partially merged state can exist. recover() completes or rolls
              back deterministically by comparing the receipt file digest to the journal.
P05 REPLACED  Controller.postmortem() and audit_anchor() aggregate reporting commands.
              Replaced by the read-only status / plan / audit commands, which never create the state directory.
P06 REPLACED  predecessor_checkpoint() as a separate checkpoint concept.
              Folded into the lineage fingerprint so that predecessor drift and graph drift invalidate through one mechanism.

--- REJECTED ---------------------------------------------------------------
X01 REJECTED  _heal_out_of_scope_contamination(): silently reverting a node's out-of-scope writes and continuing.
              An out-of-scope write is now a terminal, immutable attempt failure (failed.json, WRITE_SET_VIOLATION) before any
              merge is journaled. Run 26 recorded 3 write-set violations that the controller absorbed.
X02 REJECTED  _copy_workspace(): a full copytree sandbox per attempt.
              This produced the concurrent-main-workspace conflict in PM-19 and made attempts expensive. Run 27 attempts hold
              metadata and logs only; the node writes into the repository directly and the controller validates and receipts.
X03 REJECTED  PatchStore, create_overlay(), revoke(), effective_prompt(): mutating a node's effective prompt through an overlay
              chain. Run 26 needed 14 immutable patches. In Run 27 a prompt is a frozen input whose digest is bound into the
              lineage fingerprint, so changing a prompt invalidates the node and every descendant instead of being patched around.
X04 REJECTED  adopt_v2() and rebase(): in-place manifest/graph migration commands.
              A graph edit now simply invalidates every admitted receipt (proven by
              tests/test_run27_controller.py::test_a_graph_edit_invalidates_the_whole_admitted_chain).
X05 REJECTED  run_generation(), _run_isolated(), _prompt_packet(), terminate_active_processes(), ACTIVE_PROCESSES_LOCK:
              spawning and signal-killing model subprocesses. Run 26 disclosed that controller subprocesses were killed by an
              outside mechanism and completed work was later mechanically re-admitted. The Run 27 controller launches no model
              process at all; it only validates, verifies, and receipts. External kills are handled by the named readmit path.
X06 REJECTED  select_disjoint(): parallel ready-node selection. rules.allow_parallel_ready_nodes is false and
              tools/validate_plan.py enforces it.
X07 REJECTED  preflight(), _evaluate_preflight(), _parse_claude_json_envelope(): provider preflight and Claude envelope parsing.
              Out of scope for the implementation scheduler; the production preflight belongs to N30.
X08 REJECTED  _blocked_result() synthesising a BLOCKED receipt. A BLOCKED node result never produces a receipt at all; the
              attempt fails with OUTCOME_NOT_ADMISSIBLE and is preserved.
X09 REJECTED  _missing_required_outputs() as a post-merge check. Final outputs are digested at admission time into
              receipt.final_outputs and are a standing currency condition thereafter, not a one-shot check.

--- EVIDENCE PROVENANCE ----------------------------------------------------
The Run 26 537-event audit stream is NOT evidence for this controller. It is the record of the defective controller described
in PM-19 (41 attempt creations, 22 BLOCKED events, 9 controller_failed events, 9 claude_failed reasons, 9 inadmissible-status
reasons, 5 merge rollbacks, 3 write-set violations, one externally interrupted merge). No Run 26 event, receipt, attempt, or
patch is cited as passing evidence anywhere in this node's result. The only evidence for the Run 27 controller is the 80-test
suite in this node's own three test files and the command logs in this evidence directory.
